        "Sajeev John",
        "Susumu Noda"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Photonic crystals established a powerful way to control light through periodic structure, including the possibility of photonic band gaps, and shaped modern optics and nanophotonics.",
        "attribution": "Yablonovitch and John made seminal early contributions; Noda helped establish practical photonic-crystal devices.",
        "maturity": "The core physics is well established, and the field has produced sustained research and applications.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The ballot spans several strands of photonic-crystal work, including Russell's distinct contributions to photonic-crystal fibers, so a narrow laureate selection needs care."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
