      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Detecting high-energy astrophysical neutrinos opened a new observational window on the universe and established neutrinos as probes of extreme cosmic sources.",
        "attribution": "Halzen was a leading architect and advocate of IceCube, while Karle and Spiering made major contributions to the detector and the collaboration's development.",
        "maturity": "The discovery is supported by a substantial body of observations, though source identification and the field's full scientific reach continue to develop.",
